From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 15:23:58 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] libxess: Add stand-ins for Intel's XeSS libraries.

XeSS's path for GPUs other than Intel's (DP4a) is built on 8-bit dot
products that Apple GPUs don't have; DXMT's airconv emulates each one
(Dot4AddI8Packed/U8Packed), and SMITE 2 with XeSS ran at ~3.8 FPS on
every translator (DXMT 3.80, Rosetta+DXMT 3.82, D3DMetal 3.82; ~250 ms
of GPU compute per frame), against ~36 FPS with another upscaler. A
fresh prefix makes XeSS SMITE 2's default, so a new player gets 4 FPS.

Add builtin libxess.dll and libxess_dx11.dll exporting the functions of
the libraries games ship, in their order: the 72 and 51 exports of
SMITE 2's XeSS SDK 2.0.1.41 libraries, read from their export tables.
They cover every function the public XeSS 1.x/2.0 headers declare
(xess.h, xess_d3d12.h, xess_d3d11.h, xess_vk.h and their _debug.h), so
no other export is added. A game importing either library statically
still starts.

- xessGetVersion reports 2.0.1 (XESS_RESULT_SUCCESS).
- xessD3D12CreateContext, xessD3D11CreateContext and
  xessVKCreateContext store a NULL context and return
  XESS_RESULT_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED_DEVICE (-1 in the public xess.h).
- The capability calls (xessIsOptimalDriver, the AIL calls, the Vulkan
  and Trinity requirement queries, xessTrinityCreateContext) and Intel's
  driver-extension entries (INTC_*, whose signatures aren't public)
  return the same without reading their arguments.
- xessDestroyContext(NULL) succeeds; every other call takes a context,
  none exists, and it returns XESS_RESULT_ERROR_INVALID_CONTEXT (-8)
  without reading its arguments.

Games then fall back to FSR or TSR. Both modules are built like
msvcp140 (ARM64X: arm64ec, which x64 code loads, and aarch64). The
launcher selects them with WINEDLLOVERRIDES libxess,libxess_dx11=b
unless MACNEUTRON_XESS=1, which restores the game's own XeSS.

Registered in configure.ac and in the configure these patches carry,
by hand as patch 0016 does (no autoreconf).

Local to MacNeutron; not proposed upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
